Welcome home. You are kitty, and /usr/kitty is yours.

Compile and run, for yourself:
  cc hello.c            real clang + wasm-ld, then it runs — Hello Kitty
  python hello.py       real CPython 3.14
  go                    a real Go binary (GOOS=wasip1); go explains the rest

Look around:
  ls /bin               the commands — cat, sed, grep, sort, sam, acme, and more
  ls                    your home: this README and the three hello programs
  cal                   this month
  cat /etc/motd | tr a-z A-Z
  echo the quick brown fox | sed 's/quick/QUICK/' | wc

Windows and editors:
  win acme &            the real acme, in a window (option-click = button 2)
  win rc &              another shell, in a window

The whole tour:
  rc /rc/tour

Everything runs in this browser tab. A reload forgets it all.
